course: dictionary
lesson: 11183
title: Wisdom
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Wisdom is a noun. It means knowing what is sensible and good, and choosing well because you have learned from experience. A clue is in the sentence: «Everyone gets older: grey hair, glasses and stiffer knees come, but so do experience and wisdom.» Experience comes with age, so wisdom must be something you gain over time.
explain: Wisdom can also mean the knowledge and good advice people pass on. «The wisdom of our grandparents» means the useful things they learned and now share with you. Stories use this idea too: the wise owl, or the old woman who gives good advice, is wise because she has seen a lot and thought hard about it.
explain: «Wisdom teeth» is a different meaning. It is a name for the last four back teeth, and they come in late, often when you are in your late teens or older. Some people never get them. Context helps again: the sentence says «the last four grown-up teeth, the wisdom teeth, come in late», so the words after the name explain it.
fact: Wisdom means good, sensible judgment that grows from knowledge and experience.
fact: «Words of wisdom» are wise things that someone says, and «conventional wisdom» means what most people believe is true.
fact: Wisdom is more than knowing facts: it is knowing how and when to use them, and listening to others.
fact: Wisdom teeth are the last four grown-up teeth, and they usually come in late. Some people never get them.
fact: «Solomon» was a king of Israel about 3,000 years ago, famous for his wisdom; historians are not sure how much of the old stories about him is history.
exercise: «Everyone gets older: grey hair, glasses and stiffer knees come, but so do experience and wisdom.» What does wisdom mean here? | Teeth that come in late | *Good, sensible judgment gained from experience | A pair of glasses | Being very old and having grey hair
exercise: «The last four grown-up teeth, the wisdom teeth, come in late, and some people never get them.» Which teeth are the wisdom teeth? | *The last four grown-up teeth at the back | The four front teeth at the top | The teeth that fall out at age 6 | The first baby teeth
exercise: «The wise owl idea comes from ancient Greece, where the owl was the bird of Athena, the goddess of wisdom.» Which goddess was the owl the bird of? | Hera | Demeter | Aphrodite | *Athena
test: «The wisdom of our grandparents» is a phrase that means which of these? | A hot drink made from grandparents | Being very loud and noisy | *Useful knowledge and good advice passed on over time | The last teeth to grow in the mouth
test: Tom says «Look before you leap» is a piece of wisdom. What does he mean? | Always go first in a race | *Think carefully before you act | Jump as high as you can | Wait for someone else to decide for you
exam: A teacher says wisdom is more than knowing facts. What does she mean? | Wisdom is memorising as many facts as possible | *Wisdom is knowing how and when to use facts, and listening to others | Wisdom is the same as having a good memory | Wisdom is only for adults, and children cannot have it
